                  <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">15–25+ years</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Regional Labor Rates</h3>
          <p>
            Where you live has a dramatic effect on professional installation costs. Floor coating labor rates in California, New York, Massachusetts, and the Pacific Northwest run 40–60% above the national average. A $2,500 quote for a two-car garage in Nashville becomes $3,500–$4,000 for the same work in San Francisco or Boston. In the Midwest and South, competitive bidding and lower labor costs push professional prices toward the lower end of the ranges cited above. Always get three quotes from local contractors; the spread between the lowest and highest bid on identical work often exceeds $1,000.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Number of Coats and Cure Time</h3>
          <p>
            Multi-coat systems require the contractor to make multiple trips or schedule multiple application days. A single-coat epoxy system can be completed in one day. A three-coat polyaspartic system with proper cure time between coats typically requires the contractor to return the following day for each subsequent coat, which means scheduling and mobilization costs are incurred multiple times. This is reflected in the higher per-square-foot price of multi-coat systems, even though the materials for each individual coat are not dramatically more expensive than a single-coat system.
          </p>
        </div>

