          <p>
            The numbers tell a clear story. On a pure cost-per-year basis, a well-executed DIY project with a high-quality coating system — particularly 100% solids or high-solids with a proper topcoat — is dramatically cheaper than any professional option over a long ownership horizon. The professional systems cost $200–$400 per year of protection while the best DIY options land at $38–$60 per year. The premium you pay for professional installation buys you certainty of outcome, warranty coverage, a better surface preparation, and your time back — not necessarily a cheaper floor over its lifetime.
