          <p>
            The one case where this math flips is if your DIY project fails early due to poor surface preparation. A DIY job that peels in 18 months costs $335 upfront plus $335 to redo after stripping — bringing your effective cost to $670 for 18 months of coverage, or roughly $448 per year, which is worse than any professional option. This is why thorough surface preparation is not optional; it's the entire basis of the DIY value proposition.
